# Public information and binding before another learner

This is a deterministic interpreter/collision study with zero neural forwards,
updates, fits, capacity changes or card-ID dispatch. Two previously untrained
source definitions are supplied as full typed input. The program is not selected
by identity: a source code only retrieves a pinned public definition. All effect
selection, quantities and references come from reviewed typed nodes and printed
mechanical fields. Source titles, IDs, paths and display annotations are excluded
by the frozen canonical frontend. Changing a supported literal changes the result;
renaming source identity/display does not.

The frozen native plan has sixteen roots. LAW_045 has own Huyang/Mina x opponent
Huyang/Mina x victim damage0/1. The opponent victim is SEC_028 with physical
ASH_066, current HP7; it has no Command/Cunning aspect and survives five damage
from damage1. Helpers' attack/defeat abilities never execute. LOF_215 has two
identical SEC_028 hosts, intended hostA/B x both hosts' damage0/1 x layout/alpha
control. Both hosts are observed. The source contains the intrinsic +1/+3 upgrade
stats and a persistent parent Saboteur effect; keyword predictions are retained
separately and do not become numeric-head or attack-behavior qualification.

Only pre-action `before`, named `refs`, `declared_intent` and `observation_refs`
enter predictions. No offers, targetAction, successful commit, final parent,
after-state, private hand or deck order enters the projector. The proposed parent
is resolved from the PRE-action public intended host. Unit entry is a prospective
consequence of the declared play when evaluating whenPlayed predicates; it is
not read from an observed after-state. Predictions are conditional on the fixed
lawful play/accept-optional/choose-intent policy, not an availability oracle.

The projector preserves named candidate order and exposes exact legacy-shaped
18 globals/34 anchor attributes plus the complete canonical source document.
The legacy source-head hash uses the intended candidate's 34 attributes, exactly
as the old gathered source head did; the legacy branch hash uses each observation
anchor's own34. These are raw feature/serialization collision hashes, not a new
checkpoint forward or a claim that old vocabularies encode these new programs.
The repaired view adds full public traits/aspects, owner-specific public arena
aspect counts and source/intent/observation relations. IDs and named positions
are excluded from mechanical hashes; they only establish relations. Arena bags
are sorted semantically and deduplicated by physical reference, with public
arena completeness checked. Null inactive roles are not zero-valued cards.

Printed traits/aspects are sufficient only in these fixtures without trait or
aspect-changing effects. Current stats retain explicit known flags. A base or
upgrade-in-hand need not have unit physical stats; an actually consumed arena
unit field must be known. Unknown identity/owner, incomplete public arena, unknown
required metadata/stats, unsupported ability/continuation/query/cost, invalid
proposed selector/attachment or lethal/death/hook path yields UNKNOWN (all masks0).
There is no silent unknown-as-false or physical-zero substitution. Bound UNKNOWN
stops the analysis with a preserved artifact. The reviewed expression subset is
scalar const/ref, boolean/arithmetic binary, unary, conditional expressions,
hasSomeArenaUnit and literal hasSomeAspect/hasSomeTrait. Effects are damage,
literal stat modification, noAction and the reviewed persistent parent Saboteur.
Both branches of conditional expressions are validated. General conditional
effect continuations, other triggers and card/engine coverage expansion reject.

All four controls receive the same complete repaired public information except
for the explicitly separate legacy-omission view. `bound` resolves player ownership
and proposed parent/target correctly. `same-info-unbound` deliberately queries the
union of both owners' arenas and broadcasts parent/target effects to each observed
anchor. `wrong-owner` deliberately binds player to opponent but keeps public
proposed parent/target correct. Their errors test fixed reference resolution,
not learned capacity. `legacy-omission` is UNKNOWN, not a handpicked fallback.
This is conservative abstention by this rule baseline, not a claim that every
legacy predictor must abstain on every endpoint; many unchanged endpoints are
still representable. It is not an execution of the old learned checkpoint.
Legacy input-label collision groups and their deterministic L1 impossibility
bounds must be reported separately from any predictor MAE or coverage.

The earlier branch task forecast the outcome CONDITIONAL on choosing its query
candidate. The new attachment task forecasts the actual endpoint at BOTH anchors
under one declared intent. Missing intended-host information in that expanded
legacy-shaped branch contract does not retroactively establish a bug in the old
chosen-only training labels. Source-head collision hashes must not be scored
against target-head labels as though they were the same head contract.

Output order is the seven old target heads. target_allowed remains unknown: no
prompt/offeredness oracle is used. Surviving continuous anchors have removal0
and five observed numeric deltas. True no-change predictions are known zeros;
unsupported paths remain mask0. Native after-states are used only by the separate
verifier to derive labels and physical attachment/consequence evidence. The
source is frozen with pure synthetic tests before native collection; no source
changes or fallback selection may follow observed labels. The study does not
meet the separate two-independent-TRAIN-template-per-mechanic learning gate and
does not authorize neural learning or broad whole-card/deck qualification.
